# mcp-former aws (AWS CLI) domain ontology — bundled tier.
#
# AWS surface is huge (~200 services, thousands of operations). The
# wrapper uses pattern-matching (delete-*, terminate-*, *-with-force)
# rather than per-operation enumeration. The ontology stores:
#
#   protected_resource_tag — values of `Environment` tag that block
#                             destructive ops (production, prod, live)
#   destructive_op         — operation patterns
#   protected_service      — entire AWS services where deletion needs
#                             explicit override (route53, kms, ...)

# Production / live tag values — anything tagged with these resists
# destructive ops without --allow-unsafe.
<http://tardygrada.org/production> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/protected_tag> .
<http://tardygrada.org/prod> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/protected_tag> .
<http://tardygrada.org/live> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/protected_tag> .
<http://tardygrada.org/critical> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/protected_tag> .

# Destructive operation patterns (matched as prefix or whole verb)
<http://tardygrada.org/terminate_instances> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/delete_db_instance> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/delete_db_cluster> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/delete_bucket> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/delete_function> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/delete_stack> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/delete_user> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/delete_role> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/delete_policy> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/delete_table> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/delete_cluster> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/delete_repository> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/delete_log_group> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/delete_secret> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/delete_key> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .

# Patterns that combine the verb with --force / --recursive
<http://tardygrada.org/s3_rm_recursive> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .
<http://tardygrada.org/s3_rb_force> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/destructive_op> .

# Services where any mutation needs review (KMS rotation, Route53,
# IAM root-account stuff). Today we just block the mutating verbs in
# them; ramping into more granular controls is future work.
<http://tardygrada.org/route53> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/protected_service> .
<http://tardygrada.org/organizations> <http://schema.org/is_a> <http://tardygrada.org/protected_service> .
